      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "This usually happens in Obsidian when complex plugins like **Columns** or **Callout Studio** encounter a rendering conflict or a syntax error (like an unclosed tag).\n\nTry these steps to fix it:\n\n1.  **Force Reload**: Press `Ctrl + R` (Windows/Linux) or `Cmd + R` (Mac) to reload the UI.\n2.  **Toggle Source Mode**: Press `Ctrl + P` and search for \"Toggle Live Preview/Source mode\". Source mode is lighter and usually stops the freezing.\n3.  **Check Syntax**: Ensure there isn't a missing `---end-column---` or an unclosed `<div>`.\n4.  **Disable CSS Snippets**: If you have a custom CSS snippet for \"1200px width\" or \"120% zoom\", it might be conflicting with the plugin rendering. Try turning it off in **Settings > Appearance**.\n5.  **Safe Mode**: If it persists, temporarily disable Community Plugins to see if the file becomes editable again.",
